    "description": "Exploratory pilot of the matched-algorithm LDPC decoder cells: gf2-coding against AFF3CT v4.7.0, both f32 flooding normalized min-sum at factor 0.75, iteration cap 50 and syndrome stopping, on bit-identical parity-check matrices and bit-identical recorded LLRs. Its only purpose is to observe the measurement resolution of these cells; it decides nothing. Each call includes decoder construction, conversion, output and destruction. The identical timed batch is processed by both arms; latency is per batch, and throughput is frames per batch divided by batch time. Prepared 128-frame quality evidence is reused without resampling. Warm timing uses fixed fixture bank zero: the first recorded frame for matched latency and the first sixteen recorded frames for quality-compatible batch throughput. The remaining recorded frames supply quality validation, not additional timed samples. Both arms load the same recorded AList and construct their native sparse matrix and decoder inside each call; no encoder is initialized. This is recorded-AList operation version 1; prior fixture-constructor attempts are excluded from this family's resolution evidence."
